     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 36.75pt;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><span>2.<span style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;\">      <span> </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\">How\r\n many exons does your heterozygous deletion span? Have you checked whether these exons get filtered out in the QC step? Have you looked at your normalization results? You can take the log ratio of Yhat[[optK]]/Y_qc and find the corresponding samples that you\r\n know harbor the deletions.<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></div>\r\n</div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\">One sample has a heterozygous deletion of exons 2-4, another with exons 15-20, another with homozygous intron7-exon15 (only deletion detected by CODEX), and multiple samples have heterozygous or homozygous deletion\r\n spanning entron17-intron18.<u></u><u></u></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\"> </span></div>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125)\">How can I extract Yhat (very large list) and Y_qc (which row to choose?) for samples of interest?<u></u><u></u></span></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
